  "topic": "inlay_hints",
  "subtopic": "type_hints",
  "title": "Namespaces",
  "summary": "A hint names a type with the namespaces code at the hint would write, but `std`",
  "prose": "Class scopes stay, as do the namespaces inside `std` (`chrono::seconds`, `pmr::string`); a namespace around the hint or one a using-directive there brings in is left out, an anonymous one never shows. Template arguments read the same way.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "namespace std {\ntemplate <class Char>\nstruct basic_string {};\n\ntypedef basic_string<char> string;\n\nnamespace chrono {\nstruct seconds {};\n}  // namespace chrono\n}  // namespace std\n\nnamespace outer {\nnamespace inner {\n\nstruct S1 {};\nS1 make_s1();\nauto x = make_s1();\n\nstruct S2 {\n    template <typename T>\n    struct Nested {};\n};\n\nS2::Nested<int> make_nested();\nauto y = make_nested();\n\n}  // namespace inner\n\ninner::S1 make_inner();\nauto z = make_inner();\n\n}  // namespace outer\n\nnamespace lib {\nstruct Thing {};\n\ntemplate <class A, class B>\nstruct Pair {};\n\nThing make();\nPair<std::string, Thing> pair();\n}  // namespace lib\n\nnamespace {\nstruct Hidden {};\nHidden hide();\n}  // namespace\n\nstd::string name();\nstd::chrono::seconds wait();\n\nvoid use() {\n    auto inner = outer::make_inner();\n    auto thing = lib::make();\n    auto both = lib::pair();\n    auto text = name();\n    auto waited = wait();\n    auto hidden = hide();\n}\n\nnamespace app {\nusing namespace lib;\nauto thing = make();\n}  // namespace app\n",
      "markers": []
